1
00:00:05,722 --> 00:00:09,626
Heiwa Fansubs Presents:
Great Detective Conan
Challenge to Kudo Shin'ichi

2
00:00:13,697 --> 00:00:14,998
Ran!

3
00:00:18,769 --> 00:00:20,237
"Unknown Caller"

4
00:00:31,615 --> 00:00:33,483
"Ran's cell phone?"

5
00:00:46,897 --> 00:00:48,632
This date is...

6
00:00:50,333 --> 00:00:53,103
"September 17th, 2010"

7
00:00:54,071 --> 00:00:56,206
"Beika Center Building"

8
00:00:56,306 --> 00:00:59,042
Hey, will you be okay?

9
00:00:59,209 --> 00:01:00,510
It's expensive here.

10
00:01:00,610 --> 00:01:02,579
I'll be fine. Don't worry.

11
00:01:02,646 --> 00:01:03,580
"Beika Center Building
38th Floor Restaurant"

12
00:01:03,647 --> 00:01:05,248
You profligate son.

13
00:01:05,549 --> 00:01:06,616
Fool!

14
00:01:06,850 --> 00:01:10,887
I'm more the neglected son of parents whose
hobby it is to go off to foreign countries.

15
00:01:11,021 --> 00:01:12,823
"Shin'ichi's Childhood Friend
Mori Ran"

16
00:01:12,889 --> 00:01:15,092
And? What did you want to talk about?

17
00:01:15,192 --> 00:01:16,827
It's gotta be for some
incredible favor, isn't it?

18
00:01:16,827 --> 00:01:17,727
"High School Student Detective
Kudo Shin'ichi"

19
00:01:17,727 --> 00:01:18,662
Eh?

20
00:01:19,296 --> 00:01:22,065
You made reservations at
a restaurant like this one...

21
00:01:22,265 --> 00:01:25,669
That's...
because I got discounted tickets.

22
00:01:26,636 --> 00:01:29,606
What I wanted to tell you was...

23
00:01:33,310 --> 00:01:34,845
"For The Exclusive Use of
Authorized Personnel Only
Elevator"

24
00:01:34,878 --> 00:01:36,079
"Beika Center Building
38th Floor Office Area"

25
00:01:36,146 --> 00:01:37,380
I'll ask you to take care of the rest.

26
00:01:37,447 --> 00:01:40,317
Eh? President, aren't you going to
the company's Founding Party?

27
00:01:40,350 --> 00:01:42,285
Ah, I'm not feeling well.

28
00:01:42,352 --> 00:01:45,355
"Games Company President - Tatsumi Taiji"
I'll just stop by the company
for a bit then head home.

29
00:01:45,455 --> 00:01:46,289
"Games Executive President - Miki Yoshihisa
Games Managing Director - Hashimoto Kyoshi"

30
00:01:46,356 --> 00:01:48,825
But you said you wanted to announce
our company's long-awaited new character.

31
00:01:48,859 --> 00:01:53,330
Well, please tell everyone to do
their utmost for our company. Okay?

32
00:01:53,897 --> 00:01:56,766
Still, it's awfully dark in here.

33
00:01:57,501 --> 00:02:00,537
"Games Director - Ooba Satoru"
As part of the production,
I asked them to overdo diming the lights.

34
00:02:00,637 --> 00:02:03,507
Ahh... I see, I see.

35
00:02:07,277 --> 00:02:09,713
So long.
I'm counting on all of you.

36
00:02:10,046 --> 00:02:11,715
- Thanks for your hard work.
- Thanks for your hard work.

37
00:02:13,150 --> 00:02:14,217
I'm sorry.

38
00:02:14,251 --> 00:02:15,318
"President's Daughter
Tatsumi Sakurako"

39
00:02:15,385 --> 00:02:17,687
Do you know which restaurant
the meeting is being held in?

40
00:02:17,787 --> 00:02:19,556
Ah, it's you, Miss!

41
00:02:19,756 --> 00:02:23,293
The meeting place is in the back room of
our usual Italian restaurant.

42
00:02:23,493 --> 00:02:26,796
The lady and I are to give the congratulatory
speech at the party in a little while...

43
00:02:26,796 --> 00:02:28,532
...so could you head over there for now?

44
00:02:28,765 --> 00:02:31,601
Since the party is about to start,
don't be late.

45
00:02:31,668 --> 00:02:32,969
Yes.

46
00:02:44,381 --> 00:02:46,216
Ooba-san!

47
00:02:46,983 --> 00:02:48,685
Aren't you late?

48
00:02:48,818 --> 00:02:51,855
You promised to meet here
at half past 8, didn't you?

49
00:02:51,988 --> 00:02:53,857
Sorry, I got delayed.

50
00:02:54,057 --> 00:02:56,126
The preparations look longer than expected.

51
00:02:57,160 --> 00:02:58,695
More importantly...

52
00:02:58,895 --> 00:03:01,798
...did you have that talk with
Papa about us?

53
00:03:01,898 --> 00:03:03,266
Of course.

54
00:03:03,433 --> 00:03:05,235
He gave us the OK right off.

55
00:03:05,535 --> 00:03:08,138
Then we can be together, can't we?

56
00:03:08,205 --> 00:03:09,372
Yeah.

57
00:03:10,073 --> 00:03:14,477
Shouldn't my courage
be rewarded with a prize?

58
00:03:15,612 --> 00:03:18,848
One of your hot kisses will do.

59
00:03:33,697 --> 00:03:35,565
"Beika Center Building - 38th Floor Party Hall"
What a magnificent ceremony! Thank you very much!

60
00:03:35,899 --> 00:03:38,868
Please enjoy yourselves
to your heart's content, today!

61
00:03:43,240 --> 00:03:46,343
Ah, seems the party's started.

62
00:03:46,810 --> 00:03:50,247
At 8:30 sharp.

63
00:03:51,381 --> 00:03:53,416
Before the party...

64
00:03:53,583 --> 00:03:55,285
Here, a present.

65
00:03:55,385 --> 00:03:57,120
Eh? What is it?

66
00:03:57,354 --> 00:04:02,592
It's a pink pearl necklace that should perfectly
match the earrings you have on right now.

67
00:04:02,726 --> 00:04:04,594
Thank you!

68
00:04:04,661 --> 00:04:06,529
It's only natural.

69
00:04:06,663 --> 00:04:09,966
Well, let's go to the party;
everyone's waiting.

70
00:04:15,138 --> 00:04:16,139
And?

71
00:04:16,373 --> 00:04:17,974
What did you want to talk about?

72
00:04:18,074 --> 00:04:20,443
Eh? Ah!

73
00:04:20,910 --> 00:04:22,445
That's...

74
00:04:22,846 --> 00:04:24,748
Let's see...

75
00:04:25,048 --> 00:04:26,883
For pete's sake.

76
00:04:28,084 --> 00:04:30,353
I know it must be hard to say it...

77
00:04:30,487 --> 00:04:33,556
...but a man has to say these things
like a man!

78
00:04:36,359 --> 00:04:38,461
That you've forgotten your wallet.

79
00:04:38,962 --> 00:04:39,796
Huh?

80
00:04:39,896 --> 00:04:42,365
Eh? I'm wrong?

81
00:04:42,499 --> 00:04:46,936
After all, you've been sweating
and fidgeting for quite a while now...

82
00:04:47,937 --> 00:04:49,606
Truth is, you're right.

83
00:04:49,673 --> 00:04:51,408
It was tough telling you.

84
00:04:51,841 --> 00:04:53,376
I knew it!

85
00:04:54,911 --> 00:04:56,813
It couldn't be that, now could it?

86
00:04:57,213 --> 00:04:58,348
Eh?

87
00:04:58,515 --> 00:05:00,350
Well then...

88
00:05:00,684 --> 00:05:06,323
...here's an introduction to our company's
newest character, Kumakki-chan!

89
00:05:07,023 --> 00:05:08,191
"Kumakki"

90
00:05:10,860 --> 00:05:14,230
Kumakki-chan is winking at you!

91
00:05:14,864 --> 00:05:18,168
Because there was something
I wanted to tell you...

92
00:05:19,836 --> 00:05:23,039
...that's why I intentionally
asked you to dinner...

93
00:05:24,240 --> 00:05:25,909
That is...

94
00:05:27,210 --> 00:05:28,945
That's to say...

95
00:05:34,484 --> 00:05:35,852
Kyaa!

96
00:05:35,919 --> 00:05:38,154
What was that scream just now?

97
00:05:38,955 --> 00:05:41,491
Most likely someone found
a cockroach, isn't it?

98
00:05:41,558 --> 00:05:42,559
Nothing to worry about.

99
00:05:42,625 --> 00:05:45,762
Oi! Someone was found dead in the elevator.

100
00:05:47,897 --> 00:05:50,266
So, what I wanted to say was...

101
00:05:50,300 --> 00:05:51,167
Have they called the police?

102
00:05:51,201 --> 00:05:52,736
It's a gun! A gun!

103
00:05:52,802 --> 00:05:56,172
The President of Games
was shot through the head!

104
00:06:02,011 --> 00:06:04,614
That is, well...

105
00:06:05,715 --> 00:06:07,584
Don't force yourself.

106
00:06:07,917 --> 00:06:08,952
Eh?

107
00:06:09,052 --> 00:06:12,088
Can't be helped if
you're interested in that case.

108
00:06:12,489 --> 00:06:14,090
No...

109
00:06:16,059 --> 00:06:20,296
Hurry and get going, Detective-san.

110
00:06:22,766 --> 00:06:24,134
Sorry.

111
00:06:24,200 --> 00:06:26,136
I'll be right back!

112
00:06:33,576 --> 00:06:35,211
This was a showy one, wasn't it?

113
00:06:35,311 --> 00:06:38,348
Most likely done at close range, wasn't it?

114
00:06:38,815 --> 00:06:40,450
And? What's the victim's ID?

115
00:06:40,583 --> 00:06:43,153
Tatsumi Taiji-san, 58 years old.

116
00:06:43,353 --> 00:06:46,689
He's said to be the President of
the gaming company, Games, here in this building.

117
00:06:46,790 --> 00:06:49,426
He was discovered by these two.

118
00:06:50,527 --> 00:06:53,730
The corpse was found when
they realized they had forgotten...

119
00:06:53,797 --> 00:06:57,567
...the flowers to be used at the company's
party and were going back by this elevator.

120
00:06:57,634 --> 00:06:58,635
"MPD Investigation Unit One - Sato Miwako"
"Exclusive Use Elevator"

121
00:06:58,701 --> 00:07:01,771
This elevator is for
the exclusive use of Games, isn't it?

122
00:07:01,838 --> 00:07:02,906
That's right.

123
00:07:03,006 --> 00:07:07,510
Perhaps someone came into the building
and was hiding out on a lower floor...

124
00:07:07,577 --> 00:07:09,145
His clothes are in disarray...

125
00:07:09,212 --> 00:07:14,717
...so the criminal waited for the party
to clear so they could target someone rich...

126
00:07:15,485 --> 00:07:16,753
Huh?

127
00:07:18,087 --> 00:07:23,359
I heard from Inspector Megure about a similar
case as this one that happened here before...

128
00:07:23,393 --> 00:07:23,960
Eh?

129
00:07:23,993 --> 00:07:28,431
I'm very sorry.
I don't think this crime had money as its target.

130
00:07:29,065 --> 00:07:29,833
Eh?!

131
00:07:29,899 --> 00:07:33,503
If the criminal's goal was money
and they possessed a gun...

132
00:07:33,570 --> 00:07:36,906
...they would have taken this guy out
to some lonely area.

133
00:07:37,106 --> 00:07:40,543
If after killing him they intended to
search him for things of value...

134
00:07:40,643 --> 00:07:44,614
...the inside of a moving elevator makes for
the worst place to do that.

135
00:07:44,681 --> 00:07:46,015
Moreover...

136
00:07:46,583 --> 00:07:49,786
...even if you said the criminal
was checking through his clothes...

137
00:07:49,986 --> 00:07:52,689
...they wouldn't have bothered
to unbutton his shirt sleeve...

138
00:07:52,889 --> 00:07:54,257
Don't you think so?

139
00:07:54,324 --> 00:07:56,259
Kudo-kun?!

140
00:07:57,260 --> 00:07:59,562
Ran and I are having dinner here.

141
00:07:59,696 --> 00:08:02,665
Can two high school students
go on a date at a building...

142
00:08:02,799 --> 00:08:03,800
...with such an expensive restaurant in it?

143
00:08:03,867 --> 00:08:06,936
Well...
There's a reason why we chose here.

144
00:08:07,103 --> 00:08:08,471
Papa!

145
00:08:09,038 --> 00:08:12,141
Papa! Papa! Papa!

146
00:08:12,275 --> 00:08:13,576
Kyaa!!

147
00:08:13,776 --> 00:08:16,713
You were the last ones to see
President Tatsumi, weren't you?

148
00:08:16,846 --> 00:08:21,217
The three of us came with him
to see him off at this elevator.

149
00:08:21,451 --> 00:08:23,486
After that, his daughter came along...

150
00:08:23,686 --> 00:08:27,690
...and after the two of us briefly went over the
congratulatory speech, we went on to the party...

151
00:08:27,790 --> 00:08:31,027
Do you know around what time that was?

152
00:08:31,127 --> 00:08:33,029
Let's see... That was...

153
00:08:33,062 --> 00:08:34,464
Half past 8!

154
00:08:34,597 --> 00:08:36,766
The party crackers had started popping...

155
00:08:36,833 --> 00:08:39,536
...and because the clock hand said so,
there's no mistake about it.

156
00:08:39,636 --> 00:08:41,170
"Clock hand"?

157
00:08:41,237 --> 00:08:43,306
You're not wearing a wristwatch, are you?

158
00:08:43,439 --> 00:08:45,842
I saw the dial on Ooba-san's watch.

159
00:08:46,109 --> 00:08:48,711
When he was touching my earrings.

160
00:08:49,145 --> 00:08:51,147
He touched your earrings?

161
00:08:51,247 --> 00:08:53,716
He gave me a present here.

162
00:08:53,816 --> 00:08:54,884
"Here, a present."

163
00:08:54,984 --> 00:08:59,188
He said it was a pink pearl necklace,
the same as my earrings.

164
00:08:59,556 --> 00:09:02,759
It was for the anniversary of
the two of us being together...

165
00:09:04,827 --> 00:09:07,797
For such a thing to happen to Papa...

166
00:09:14,837 --> 00:09:16,205
Here, some water.

167
00:09:16,406 --> 00:09:18,007
Thank you.

168
00:09:20,109 --> 00:09:23,313
Um... There's something strange about
what you said earlier.

169
00:09:23,613 --> 00:09:26,015
Is it true you looked at his watch dial?

170
00:09:26,316 --> 00:09:29,652
How rude. I did look at it.

171
00:09:30,486 --> 00:09:31,821
Ah...

172
00:09:31,955 --> 00:09:36,259
Because it was so dim there when she arrived,
she couldn't have seen it, right?

173
00:09:36,926 --> 00:09:42,465
But the hands of my watch have a luminous paint
on them so they're visible even in the dark.

174
00:09:43,132 --> 00:09:46,102
The Hall was dimmed on
the President's orders.

175
00:09:46,202 --> 00:09:48,705
It was one of the details I heard
was done for the sake of the production...

176
00:09:48,738 --> 00:09:50,373
In that case, this is strange.

177
00:09:50,473 --> 00:09:53,576
Wait.
What on earth is so strange about it?

178
00:09:54,177 --> 00:09:55,311
Because, look...

179
00:09:55,345 --> 00:09:59,282
If you were touching her earrings with your
watch hand, she couldn't have seen the dial.

180
00:09:59,515 --> 00:10:01,284
You're a fool.

181
00:10:01,517 --> 00:10:04,087
When touching her ear from this side,
she could see it, couldn't she?

182
00:10:04,253 --> 00:10:05,455
Ehh...

183
00:10:05,555 --> 00:10:07,757
To her ear on your right, huh?

184
00:10:07,957 --> 00:10:10,159
When she saw that, she'd know.

185
00:10:10,326 --> 00:10:13,096
I could see her earring on
the ear to my right.

186
00:10:13,162 --> 00:10:13,997
That's why I...

187
00:10:14,030 --> 00:10:15,531
What were you doing with your right hand?

188
00:10:15,632 --> 00:10:18,067
It would have been easier to touch her
with your right hand.

189
00:10:18,935 --> 00:10:22,438
Well, if your right hand was occupied
with something else...

190
00:10:22,538 --> 00:10:24,007
...it would have been impossible to do that.

191
00:10:24,107 --> 00:10:25,475
Then what is it?

192
00:10:25,541 --> 00:10:29,145
Do you mean I had a gun in my right hand?

193
00:10:29,212 --> 00:10:30,747
A gun?

194
00:10:31,481 --> 00:10:34,684
I didn't say a single word about that.

195
00:10:43,693 --> 00:10:47,230
"What's so important that
Shin'ichi wanted to talk to me about?"

196
00:10:47,430 --> 00:10:48,965
"What is it? What could it be?!"

197
00:10:49,032 --> 00:10:50,967
Have you...

198
00:10:51,567 --> 00:10:54,037
...gained weight recently?

199
00:10:54,637 --> 00:10:55,805
Ah...

200
00:10:56,139 --> 00:10:57,507
"That's possible..."

201
00:10:57,807 --> 00:11:00,810
"My waist has gotten a little bad recently."

202
00:11:01,411 --> 00:11:07,250
"But he wouldn't have expressly
asked me out to dinner to tell me that."

203
00:11:07,617 --> 00:11:08,751
Thank you for waiting.

204
00:11:08,785 --> 00:11:10,219
Ah, um...

205
00:11:10,319 --> 00:11:14,023
Could you hold off on dessert
until my companion returns?

206
00:11:14,090 --> 00:11:16,092
He heard a scream earlier
and went flying off to it.

207
00:11:16,159 --> 00:11:17,660
But since he's a detective...

208
00:11:17,794 --> 00:11:22,298
...I think he'll probably settle it quickly
and come right back.

209
00:11:24,467 --> 00:11:26,135
Certainly.

210
00:11:27,737 --> 00:11:28,871
Um...

211
00:11:29,005 --> 00:11:30,306
What is it?

212
00:11:30,406 --> 00:11:32,642
Ah, I'm sorry.

213
00:11:32,775 --> 00:11:35,144
It's just that you're like...

214
00:11:35,244 --> 00:11:39,182
...the legendary couple
the former sommelier told me about.

215
00:11:39,315 --> 00:11:41,818
Eh? Legendary couple?

216
00:11:41,884 --> 00:11:42,919
Yeah.

217
00:11:43,119 --> 00:11:45,488
It was at this exact seat and table, too.

218
00:11:45,755 --> 00:11:48,691
It was a story from about
20 years ago, though.

219
00:11:48,758 --> 00:11:50,393
Seems the man 20 years ago
heard a scream...

220
00:11:50,460 --> 00:11:53,362
...and said that after he had solved the case
and returned, he had something to tell her...

221
00:11:53,496 --> 00:11:55,932
So it would be best if you
resolved yourself, as well.

222
00:11:56,432 --> 00:11:58,067
Something to tell her...

223
00:11:58,267 --> 00:12:01,237
To propose. A proposal.

224
00:12:01,604 --> 00:12:05,274
Pro... proposal!?

225
00:12:05,374 --> 00:12:06,809
Good luck.

226
00:12:11,013 --> 00:12:13,049
I'm sure your boyfriend did...

227
00:12:15,885 --> 00:12:16,652
Huh?

228
00:12:16,719 --> 00:12:20,890
He knew about that episode from 20 years ago
and so reserved these seats expressly.

229
00:12:20,957 --> 00:12:22,892
This is a nice production, isn't it?

230
00:12:23,626 --> 00:12:26,028
Ah, excuse me for this.

231
00:12:26,162 --> 00:12:29,899
I interjected myself only because
it was so charming.

232
00:12:31,534 --> 00:12:33,836
Ah, no...

233
00:12:41,677 --> 00:12:43,346
"Don't tell me..."

234
00:12:43,746 --> 00:12:45,848
"Don't tell me Shin'ichi will...?"

235
00:12:49,385 --> 00:12:51,287
"There's no way."

236
00:12:53,055 --> 00:12:54,157
Say.

237
00:12:54,323 --> 00:12:57,160
It seems like you're suspicious of Ooba-san.

238
00:12:57,426 --> 00:13:00,696
Since the three of saw
Papa off at the elevator...

239
00:13:00,797 --> 00:13:02,698
...it'd be impossible for Ooba-san
to commit this crime.

240
00:13:02,865 --> 00:13:06,302
Because he and I spent the entire time
afterwards at the party together.

241
00:13:06,469 --> 00:13:08,304
You didn't stop off anywhere?

242
00:13:08,471 --> 00:13:10,907
In order to put on
the necklace he'd given me...

243
00:13:11,007 --> 00:13:12,375
...I went to the restroom.

244
00:13:12,475 --> 00:13:15,545
Since I also corrected my lipstick,
it took me about 2 or 3 minutes.

245
00:13:15,645 --> 00:13:18,447
Because we talked the entire time across a wall,
it was the same as if we had been together.

246
00:13:18,514 --> 00:13:20,616
"I'm happy that you're pleased with it."

247
00:13:21,417 --> 00:13:22,585
Detective Takagi!

248
00:13:23,085 --> 00:13:26,756
A gun with a silencer and an empty cartridge
were found where the building collects its trash.

249
00:13:26,856 --> 00:13:27,924
What?

250
00:13:28,858 --> 00:13:30,993
Is there a trash chute on this floor?

251
00:13:31,027 --> 00:13:31,928
Yes.

252
00:13:32,395 --> 00:13:34,297
Next to the restrooms.

253
00:13:34,463 --> 00:13:35,698
I see.

254
00:13:35,832 --> 00:13:38,434
Without having to separate from her,
that's where he got rid of it.

255
00:13:38,534 --> 00:13:40,136
Oi, oi.

256
00:13:40,336 --> 00:13:43,639
Seems you guys are out
to make me the criminal.

257
00:13:43,773 --> 00:13:46,909
In that case,
please explain to me how it was...

258
00:13:46,976 --> 00:13:51,080
...that I killed the President while
he was going down the elevator.

259
00:13:51,814 --> 00:13:56,085
And since she and I were together
the entire time...

260
00:13:56,319 --> 00:13:58,287
...even if I had taken a shot at him...

261
00:13:58,387 --> 00:14:01,858
...wouldn't you find traces
of gunpowder on my cuffs?

262
00:14:01,924 --> 00:14:04,060
Well then, let us have a look.

263
00:14:04,160 --> 00:14:06,062
Yes, I don't mind.

264
00:14:06,162 --> 00:14:08,231
You won't find it anyway.

265
00:14:09,932 --> 00:14:11,234
This way.

266
00:14:13,269 --> 00:14:15,071
Ooba-san...

267
00:14:17,373 --> 00:14:21,143
Um... Did you two kiss?

268
00:14:21,377 --> 00:14:22,211
Eh?

269
00:14:22,245 --> 00:14:23,980
My mother told me this.

270
00:14:24,247 --> 00:14:28,851
"A lady corrects her lipstick
after a meal or a kiss."

271
00:14:29,652 --> 00:14:32,655
And so... how did he do it that time?

272
00:14:32,955 --> 00:14:34,423
"How"?

273
00:14:34,824 --> 00:14:37,460
He put his arm around me like this.

274
00:14:39,629 --> 00:14:41,530
No, no, no! Kudo-kun!

275
00:14:41,664 --> 00:14:44,800
At that time...
was your back to the elevator?

276
00:14:44,967 --> 00:14:47,003
Yes, it was...

277
00:14:48,337 --> 00:14:51,040
Are you two always doing things secretly?

278
00:14:51,407 --> 00:14:52,575
Yes.

279
00:14:52,742 --> 00:14:55,511
We had also arranged to meet
over at his place tonight, too.

280
00:14:57,346 --> 00:14:58,981
Miss...

281
00:15:00,416 --> 00:15:03,819
We hate to be rude, but it's time to go.

282
00:15:09,258 --> 00:15:12,495
Ah, excuse me.
Just one more question...

283
00:15:14,330 --> 00:15:18,501
Could it be those earrings were
a gift from Ooba-san, too?

284
00:15:18,701 --> 00:15:20,169
Sorry to disappoint you.

285
00:15:20,369 --> 00:15:23,372
These were an impulse buy I made
just before coming here.

286
00:15:23,506 --> 00:15:25,007
They weren't a present.

287
00:15:31,480 --> 00:15:33,649
It was like I thought...

288
00:15:34,250 --> 00:15:38,821
The President was definitely shot by Ooba-san.

289
00:15:39,021 --> 00:15:42,191
There are just two questions left...

290
00:15:44,126 --> 00:15:47,997
"The President's strange behavior
in the elevator..."

291
00:15:48,064 --> 00:15:50,099
"...and the traces of gunpowder."

292
00:15:50,933 --> 00:15:55,738
"From his ample attitude of self-confidence
that no trace of gunpowder will turn up..."

293
00:15:55,938 --> 00:15:57,940
"...he must have had some kind of trick."

294
00:15:59,442 --> 00:16:00,576
Kudo-kun.

295
00:16:00,676 --> 00:16:04,647
At the time of the party, Ooba-san had to
take off his suit to get into a cartoon costume.

296
00:16:04,780 --> 00:16:06,849
Cartoon costume? Ooba-san?

297
00:16:06,949 --> 00:16:07,883
Yes.

298
00:16:07,917 --> 00:16:12,054
Tonight's party was also a meeting
to announce a new character for the company...

299
00:16:12,154 --> 00:16:14,957
...so he was on-stage in that
cartoon costume the entire time.

300
00:16:14,991 --> 00:16:18,094
We were all surprised when it
turned out Director Ooba was in it.

301
00:16:18,194 --> 00:16:20,663
The Director worked hard
to make it popular, didn't he?

302
00:16:20,763 --> 00:16:21,964
He was making it wink repeatedly.

303
00:16:22,031 --> 00:16:25,735
It was popular at first, but that reversed
and became boring when that was all he did.

304
00:16:26,135 --> 00:16:29,772
Excuse me.
Could you show me this cartoon costume?

305
00:16:33,709 --> 00:16:34,677
This is it?

306
00:16:34,810 --> 00:16:36,045
Yes.

307
00:16:36,412 --> 00:16:38,047
Who was in charge of the party?

308
00:16:38,147 --> 00:16:39,682
Director Ooba.

309
00:16:50,626 --> 00:16:52,094
I see...

310
00:16:52,194 --> 00:16:53,662
That's how it was done.

311
00:16:53,696 --> 00:16:55,231
Have you found out something?

312
00:16:55,398 --> 00:16:57,900
Yes, pretty much.

313
00:16:58,067 --> 00:16:59,502
Assistant Inspector!

314
00:16:59,935 --> 00:17:02,505
No traces of gunpowder were found
on Ooba-san's clothing.

315
00:17:02,638 --> 00:17:04,106
Ah... I see.

316
00:17:04,173 --> 00:17:07,209
Then I guess this case was a criminal
from outside looking for money.

317
00:17:07,376 --> 00:17:11,180
Get information about any suspicious persons
coming or leaving the building during the party.

318
00:17:11,247 --> 00:17:12,381
No...

319
00:17:12,581 --> 00:17:14,116
That won't be necessary.

320
00:17:14,216 --> 00:17:15,217
Eh?

321
00:17:15,418 --> 00:17:18,521
The criminal is already in our hands...

322
00:17:18,721 --> 00:17:20,790
Now, shall we go up?

323
00:17:20,890 --> 00:17:24,293
Up to the stage to explain what the truth is.

324
00:17:25,261 --> 00:17:27,563
Oi! What do you intend by this?

325
00:17:27,963 --> 00:17:32,501
Why am I being called in again
as a suspect in the President's murder?

326
00:17:32,735 --> 00:17:36,038
I told you that Ooba-san and I
were together the entire time, didn't I?

327
00:17:36,105 --> 00:17:37,973
Why don't you believe me?

328
00:17:38,074 --> 00:17:39,809
I don't doubt you.

329
00:17:39,942 --> 00:17:44,146
I think you and Ooba-san
were together the entire time.

330
00:17:44,313 --> 00:17:45,881
It was while at your side...

331
00:17:45,981 --> 00:17:48,484
...that the moment of the crime occurred.

332
00:17:48,751 --> 00:17:50,152
At that time...

333
00:17:50,252 --> 00:17:55,658
...you had your eyes closed and your back to
the elevator to exchange a kiss with Ooba-san.

334
00:17:56,025 --> 00:17:58,227
Ki... A kiss?

335
00:17:59,195 --> 00:18:03,799
Like this, holding your head with
his left arm and blocking off your ears...

336
00:18:03,866 --> 00:18:07,336
...he simultaneously kissed you
while pressing the elevator button...

337
00:18:09,071 --> 00:18:10,506
The moment the door opened...

338
00:18:10,573 --> 00:18:14,643
...your father was shot to death
using a gun with a silencer.

339
00:18:16,846 --> 00:18:18,914
By Ooba-san's hand.

340
00:18:20,549 --> 00:18:25,121
Even if you say he blocked off her ears
and shot him with a silenced gun...

341
00:18:25,221 --> 00:18:29,024
...if a person was shot and collapsed,
wouldn't you hear at least a little of the sound?

342
00:18:29,125 --> 00:18:32,995
So I think she would have heard
a faint sound.

343
00:18:33,329 --> 00:18:38,767
That's why the moment when Ooba-san fired
was just before the party began.

344
00:18:40,970 --> 00:18:44,240
The sound of noisy crackers going off
along with the start of the party...

345
00:18:44,740 --> 00:18:47,743
...combined with him covering her ears...

346
00:18:50,112 --> 00:18:52,181
"Seems the party has started."

347
00:18:52,281 --> 00:18:55,751
A faint sound just before that wouldn't
have made much of an impression on her.

348
00:18:57,086 --> 00:18:59,455
Those are some
interesting things you're saying.

349
00:18:59,488 --> 00:19:04,326
However...
There's one big hole in your reasoning.

350
00:19:06,095 --> 00:19:10,299
Since the President was going home,
why was he still in the elevator?

351
00:19:10,733 --> 00:19:14,837
Don't tell me he remained in the elevator
just to be killed by me?

352
00:19:14,904 --> 00:19:16,639
Exactly!

353
00:19:17,873 --> 00:19:22,444
Without going down, the President
was just waiting in the elevator instead.

354
00:19:23,379 --> 00:19:27,783
So he could put on the cartoon costume
you were going to bring there for him.

355
00:19:31,086 --> 00:19:32,388
Ooba-san.

356
00:19:32,488 --> 00:19:35,457
You probably were the one who
informed the President of it.

357
00:19:36,025 --> 00:19:39,128
"Let's surprise the staff
by having you pretend to leave..."

358
00:19:39,195 --> 00:19:42,431
"...and then secretly bring you
back into the Hall."

359
00:19:42,798 --> 00:19:45,634
Then, the reason the victim's clothes
were in disarray was...

360
00:19:46,135 --> 00:19:49,638
The President was preparing
to change into the costume.

361
00:19:50,272 --> 00:19:51,807
I see.

362
00:19:51,907 --> 00:19:53,609
If the elevator was just standing by...

363
00:19:53,709 --> 00:19:56,679
...you wouldn't have heard the arriving
"Ching" sound either, would you?

364
00:19:56,745 --> 00:19:59,815
Moreover, this elevator is for
the exclusive use of employees.

365
00:19:59,982 --> 00:20:01,817
Ooba-san had calculated...

366
00:20:01,884 --> 00:20:04,987
...that no one would be using it up here
until after the party...

367
00:20:05,054 --> 00:20:07,256
What about the traces of gunpowder?

368
00:20:07,623 --> 00:20:10,192
If I was the criminal,
that should obviously have come out.

369
00:20:10,392 --> 00:20:12,261
But unfortunately from my clothes...

370
00:20:12,294 --> 00:20:13,862
Ooba-san.

371
00:20:13,929 --> 00:20:15,698
Weren't you winking?

372
00:20:16,131 --> 00:20:17,700
The staff personnel told us about that.

373
00:20:17,800 --> 00:20:21,604
That all you did while inside
that costume was wink.

374
00:20:21,904 --> 00:20:23,839
And you were deliberate about it.

375
00:20:24,740 --> 00:20:27,776
Your goal in winking wasn't to be popular.

376
00:20:28,210 --> 00:20:32,181
It was in order for you to hide something
inside one of this costume's eyes...

377
00:20:32,314 --> 00:20:34,450
...so that it wouldn't move around.

378
00:20:37,486 --> 00:20:40,756
Inside this plastic bag are
4 rubber bands and a glove.

379
00:20:41,056 --> 00:20:43,692
In advance, you had put
into your jacket pocket...

380
00:20:43,892 --> 00:20:47,062
...a glove for your right hand
and a plastic bag for covering the gun...

381
00:20:47,196 --> 00:20:49,298
...to be fastened down with the rubber bands.

382
00:20:49,465 --> 00:20:51,300
Equipping it that way would be easy.

383
00:20:51,433 --> 00:20:54,169
And, even if you shot the gun...

384
00:20:54,303 --> 00:20:57,640
...no trace of gunpowder would get on your clothes
nor would the cartridge fall to the ground.

385
00:20:58,007 --> 00:21:02,311
But, if he was putting on
and removing such things in front of her...

386
00:21:02,344 --> 00:21:03,812
...wouldn't she have noticed?

387
00:21:03,912 --> 00:21:07,683
Of course he could do all that in plain view.

388
00:21:08,917 --> 00:21:10,486
If you would please.

389
00:21:12,121 --> 00:21:15,157
When the lights were dimmed like this...

390
00:21:15,324 --> 00:21:17,359
...his worries were cut in half.

391
00:21:17,693 --> 00:21:21,630
And this is where he presented her
with the necklace.

392
00:21:21,897 --> 00:21:23,632
Without parting from her...

393
00:21:23,732 --> 00:21:28,871
...he used the trash chute next to
the restrooms to throw away the gun.

394
00:21:30,706 --> 00:21:33,509
After that, your hands would have been bare.

395
00:21:33,676 --> 00:21:36,745
In other words,
you intentionally stuck close to her.

396
00:21:36,979 --> 00:21:40,482
This plastic bag has your fingerprints on it!

397
00:21:46,789 --> 00:21:49,758
My fingerprints are on that plastic bag?

398
00:21:51,393 --> 00:21:53,595
Then I'm in luck.

399
00:21:54,063 --> 00:21:57,299
Because I also touched that plastic bag.

400
00:21:57,566 --> 00:21:58,534
What?

401
00:21:58,600 --> 00:22:01,036
Oi! That's right, isn't it?

402
00:22:01,303 --> 00:22:02,971
Ah, yes.

403
00:22:03,072 --> 00:22:04,606
The Director told us...

404
00:22:04,640 --> 00:22:07,576
..."Since if you opened it,
this one eye won't shut..."

405
00:22:07,710 --> 00:22:13,215
"...and since it may contain important parts
for the costume, just put it in as is."

406
00:22:13,349 --> 00:22:15,884
Here's MY deduction.

407
00:22:16,218 --> 00:22:18,520
Someone with a grudge against me...

408
00:22:18,687 --> 00:22:23,225
...took the opportunity to kill the President on a
lower floor while she and I were at the restroom...

409
00:22:23,325 --> 00:22:27,596
...and then hid that in the costume
in order to pin the blame on me.

410
00:22:29,164 --> 00:22:32,034
I think that's far more realistic than
your nonsense fantasy talk...

411
00:22:32,101 --> 00:22:34,937
...about me shooting in the middle of a kiss...

412
00:22:35,637 --> 00:22:41,610
...and then putting that inside
the costume at the changing room...

413
00:22:41,877 --> 00:22:44,813
...before going out to the Hall.

414
00:22:45,147 --> 00:22:47,383
Now Great Detective.

415
00:22:47,516 --> 00:22:50,652
Shouldn't you end your
joke reasoning already?

416
00:22:50,719 --> 00:22:56,425
I'm extremely confident that for each of a hundred
of your foolish questions, I can return an answer.

417
00:23:00,162 --> 00:23:02,264
Now Great Detective.

418
00:23:02,398 --> 00:23:05,401
Shouldn't you end your
joke reasoning already?

419
00:23:05,634 --> 00:23:10,939
I'm extremely confident that for each of a hundred
of your foolish questions, I can return an answer.

420
00:23:14,109 --> 00:23:15,811
Pink pearls...

421
00:23:16,345 --> 00:23:17,246
Eh?

422
00:23:17,312 --> 00:23:22,151
You said that when you presented
the necklace to her, didn't you?

423
00:23:23,352 --> 00:23:27,189
"This pink pearl necklace
is the same as your earrings."

424
00:23:27,389 --> 00:23:29,057
How could you know that?

425
00:23:29,258 --> 00:23:32,294
That she had on pink pearls?

426
00:23:34,029 --> 00:23:36,432
With just look, I immediately...

427
00:23:39,968 --> 00:23:42,104
These earrings...

428
00:23:42,404 --> 00:23:46,608
...are ones she purchased on impulse
just before meeting you tonight.

429
00:23:46,875 --> 00:23:48,177
In other words...

430
00:23:48,277 --> 00:23:52,214
...that was the first time
you had seen her earrings.

431
00:23:52,614 --> 00:23:55,717
In this space of near-total darkness...

432
00:23:56,151 --> 00:23:59,154
...her pearls were nothing but black balls.

433
00:23:59,288 --> 00:24:00,789
That is, here...

434
00:24:01,156 --> 00:24:04,026
...there was no way to distinguish
that they were pink.

435
00:24:05,294 --> 00:24:06,795
Yes...

436
00:24:07,229 --> 00:24:10,466
But then while you and her
were exchanging a kiss...

437
00:24:10,866 --> 00:24:13,502
...light came from this door
when it opened, didn't it?

438
00:24:24,613 --> 00:24:27,883
Now, how do you answer this, Ooba-san?

439
00:24:28,183 --> 00:24:31,487
Why did you open this door then?

440
00:24:31,720 --> 00:24:33,322
Ooba-san...

441
00:24:34,056 --> 00:24:36,158
Why did I open it?

442
00:24:37,025 --> 00:24:39,695
There's a simple answer for that.

443
00:24:40,529 --> 00:24:42,965
I had sworn to my father.

444
00:24:43,065 --> 00:24:45,801
That I would surely get his revenge for him.

445
00:24:46,435 --> 00:24:48,203
Your father's revenge?

446
00:24:48,337 --> 00:24:52,774
My father was doing quite well
at his own gaming company.

447
00:24:53,609 --> 00:24:59,114
That is until 20 years ago when Tatsumi
approached him with talk of a merger.

448
00:24:59,615 --> 00:25:04,286
But in reality, it wasn't a merger,
but a takeover...

449
00:25:07,689 --> 00:25:10,492
My father,
who was a Vice President in name only...

450
00:25:11,360 --> 00:25:13,962
...committed suicide over
his disappointment...

451
00:25:15,130 --> 00:25:16,665
But...

452
00:25:16,798 --> 00:25:18,934
Papa was so kind to you...

453
00:25:19,001 --> 00:25:20,435
Yeah...

454
00:25:21,069 --> 00:25:24,273
He drove off the debts from
my father's death...

455
00:25:24,506 --> 00:25:28,176
...and Tatsumi promoted me
to one post after another.

456
00:25:28,544 --> 00:25:32,214
I planned this in order
to take over the company.

457
00:25:32,548 --> 00:25:33,982
No...

458
00:25:34,383 --> 00:25:36,552
It was all a game.

459
00:25:37,586 --> 00:25:41,390
There's a story where the main character
borrows some power from the Devil...

460
00:25:41,557 --> 00:25:44,459
...in order to gain revenge against a demon.

461
00:25:48,764 --> 00:25:50,399
Still...

462
00:25:50,866 --> 00:25:53,635
...it seems impossible that my father and I
would share the same ending together.

463
00:25:53,869 --> 00:25:55,771
You and your father together?

464
00:25:56,204 --> 00:26:00,709
My father committed suicide
and made it look like it was a murder.

465
00:26:01,076 --> 00:26:02,878
20 years ago...

466
00:26:03,078 --> 00:26:08,283
...he set it up to look as if
Tatsumi had killed him.

467
00:26:09,451 --> 00:26:12,387
However, that was unmasked.

468
00:26:12,588 --> 00:26:17,259
By a young man with a very sharp mind
like this one's tonight.

469
00:26:18,694 --> 00:26:22,798
It was the retaliation for having
borrowed the Devil's power.

470
00:26:26,535 --> 00:26:27,603
Here.

471
00:26:33,375 --> 00:26:34,910
Something wrong?

472
00:26:35,344 --> 00:26:36,912
I remember!

473
00:26:36,979 --> 00:26:38,447
It was Kudo Yuusaku!

474
00:26:38,480 --> 00:26:40,449
The one Inspector Megure was talking about.

475
00:26:40,549 --> 00:26:46,088
That case 20 years ago was settled by
the mystery writer, Kudo Yuusaku.

476
00:26:46,154 --> 00:26:48,790
"Kudo Yuusaku"?
This Kudo-kun's father?

477
00:26:48,924 --> 00:26:53,028
In other words, by taking over
this revenge play from his father...

478
00:26:53,128 --> 00:26:58,200
...Kudo Yuusaku and his son Shin'ichi
have now unraveled it across 2 generations.

479
00:26:59,401 --> 00:27:02,437
What an ironic ending, right, Kudo-kun...?

480
00:27:03,138 --> 00:27:05,574
Ala? Where is Kudo-kun?

481
00:27:08,443 --> 00:27:09,711
Say, have you heard?

482
00:27:09,811 --> 00:27:11,713
That incident seems to have been settled.

483
00:27:11,847 --> 00:27:13,715
Eh? Really?

484
00:27:13,915 --> 00:27:17,319
You should meet your boyfriend before long...

485
00:27:19,187 --> 00:27:22,824
He's not my boyfriend...

486
00:27:28,230 --> 00:27:30,832
Sorry... It took some time.

487
00:27:30,899 --> 00:27:32,300
Yeah.

488
00:27:44,579 --> 00:27:47,115
Say, Ran.

489
00:27:49,184 --> 00:27:50,986
Shin'ichi?

490
00:27:55,691 --> 00:27:57,092
I...

491
00:27:59,795 --> 00:28:01,596
About you...

492
00:28:10,072 --> 00:28:11,239
Eh?

493
00:28:12,808 --> 00:28:14,943
Excuse me.
The restaurant has closed already.

494
00:28:15,010 --> 00:28:18,313
Ah, I'm sorry.
We'll leave right away.

495
00:28:30,325 --> 00:28:32,027
"Elevator"

496
00:28:39,968 --> 00:28:41,136
Ran!

497
00:28:41,203 --> 00:28:42,804
Wait!

498
00:28:51,646 --> 00:28:52,981
Ran...

499
00:28:56,284 --> 00:28:58,820
"Bomb Warning and Murder Request"

500
00:28:59,554 --> 00:29:04,226
"The Conflict Between Three People's Testimony"

501
00:29:06,661 --> 00:29:09,331
"This Drama is Fictional"

